{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>After these things.</b> Because that accursed one had accustomed everyone to speak of the righteous man and to slander him, the Holy One, blessed be He, brought about the offense of these two, so that they would turn to each other and not to him — and further, so that relief would come to the righteous man through them." "<b>Sinned.</b> This one — a fly was found in his פַּיְילִי פּוֹטֵירִין, and this one — a pebble was found in his גְּלוּסְקִין." "<b>And the baking.</b> The king's bread — and the term אֲפִיָּה applies only to bread; in לַעַז: פישטו״ר."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 40, :notes {1 "Old French terms: פיילי פוטירין is identifiable as philé poterin (a type of cooked dish or cup); גלוסקין is glossed in some witnesses as a kind of baked good or biscuit, possibly related to Old French gastel/glace.", 2 "The la'az פישטו״ר corresponds to Old French pestor / pastour, related to 'pastry' or 'baked goods' (cf. modern French pâte)."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:02:48.833446889Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}